Hi Anil,

During the March inspection of pressure vessel V-200 in Unit 3, the relief valve set
pressure was measured at 18.5 bar against a design set point of 18.0 bar. Wall thickness
at the shell was 12.4 mm (minimum allowable 11.0 mm), so the vessel integrity is fine, but
the relief valve set pressure is drifting high.

Per OISD-STD-106 we should re-certify the relief valve. Can we schedule a bench test and
re-set during the next shutdown window?

